.TH tuhead n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuhead
.PP
Head\-like helpers.
.CS
package require tclutils::tuhead
puts [::tclutils::tuhead::file README.md 20]
.CE
.PP
Commands:
.IP \(bu
\fBtext text ?count?\fR \-\- the first \fBcount\fR lines (default 10)
.IP \(bu
\fBfile path ?count? ?\-encoding enc?\fR \-\- the same for a file (default utf\-8)
.PP
As with \fBhead \-n\fR, the result keeps the line ends: every line ends with \fB\en\fR, except the last line of the input when it has none. \fBtext\fR and \fBfile\fR give the same result (0.2; 0.1 \fBtext\fR took the empty rest after a final \fB\en\fR as a line, \fBfile\fR dropped every line end). A count that is not an integer >= 0 raises \fBTCLUTILS TUHEAD COUNT\fR. Print with \fBputs \-nonewline\fR.
